p_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.12388767973555748,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":89.6,"_gate_rev_durability":0.12081638632422931,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":85.4,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.036214207382552134,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":51.3,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.021559271947633962,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":76.9,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.094610006,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":63.1,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Chubb Limited provides insurance and reinsurance products worldwide. It operates in six segments: North America Commercial Property and Casualty (P&C) Insurance, North America Personal P&C Insurance, North America Agricultural Insurance, Overseas General Insurance, Global Reinsurance, and Life Insurance. The company offers property and general liability, workers' compensation, and umbrella; professional and management liability; environmental, health, and international coverages; and claims and risk management products and services, loss control, and engineering and complex claims management. It also provides homeowners, automobile and collector cars, valuable articles, and personal and excess liability insurance. In addition, the company offers multiple peril crop insurance and crop-hail insurance for farm, ranch, specialty (P&C), and commercial agriculture products; product and employer liability, business interruption, and specialty risk; property insurance products, including traditional commercial fire coverage, energy industry-related, marine, construction, and other technical coverages; personal accident and supplemental medical coverages, such as accidental death, business/holiday travel, specified disease, disability, medical and hospital indemnity, and income protection; and directors and officers, professional indemnity, cyber, surety, aviation, political risk, and specialty personal lines products. Further, it provides property catastrophe reinsurance; traditional and specialty P&C reinsurance; and protection and savings products, which includes individual and group term life, dental, critical illness, dementia, hospital cash, credit life, group employee benefits, whole life, universal life, unit linked contracts, endowment plans, and annuities. The company was formerly known as ACE Limited and changed its name to Chubb Limited in January 2016. Chubb Limited was incorporated in 1985 and is headquartered in Zurich, Switzerland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Evan G. Greenberg | Chairman & CEO | Age 70 | Compensation: $14.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 45K people. Revenue per employee of $1.3M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 9%/yr across its filed history. CEO compensation is 11\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Chubb Limited is a large-cap financial services business with a $143.6B market cap on $59.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +11% over the past three years and +12% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 12% against a 7% cost of capital, a 5-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 17\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 3.6% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 9.5% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.39075404912581935},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $24.9M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["33 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Chubb Limited $CB Shares Newly Acquired by R Squared Ltd","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/chubb-limited-cb-shares-newly-acquired-by-r-squared-ltd.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794567470.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.881,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"14,297 Chubb Limited $CB Shares Sold by Fifth Third Bancorp","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/14297-chubb-limited-cb-shares-sold-by-fifth-third-bancorp.html","date":"2026